  "name": "Jesse Kotton Sky Striker (Utopia Double)",
  "category": "curated",
  "format": "classic",
  "manual": "GLOSSARY. **MMZ** = your five Main Monster Zones. Almost every Sky Striker card reads \"If you control no monsters in your Main Monster Zone\", so ONE monster sitting there turns most of your deck off for the rest of the turn. **EMZ** = the two shared Extra Monster Zones; you may only ever occupy one of them. **Ace** = a \"Sky Striker Ace\" Link Monster. **The 3+ threshold** = the clause \"if you have 3 or more Spells in your GY\" that upgrades nearly every Sky Striker Spell. **Mine** = `Mystic Mine`. **The kill / the OTK** = the `Number 39: Utopia Double` line in its own section below. **Blind second** = a build aimed at going SECOND and breaking a board, not at setting one up.\n\nSOURCE TAGS used throughout. [JK] = Jesse Kotton explaining this exact deck card-by-card, in the post-event interview uploaded twice (TeamSamuraiX1 \"1ST PLACE WORLDS QUALIFIER: UTOPIA DOUBLE STRIKER OTK DECK PROFILE 2019 FT. JESSE KOTTON\", and Nerdy Jersey's cut of the same sit-down). [DF] = Dylan Fricker, Kotton's Game Nation teammate, profiling the SAME shell at the 2019 NAWCQ (Team Bortle). [PL] = Peter Lauziere, ARG Invitational 2019 Top 16, an independent Mystic Mine Sky Striker pilot. [YPD] = the YGOPRODeck page this list is transcribed from. [BAN] = the TCG Forbidden & Limited List in force 29 Apr - 14 Jul 2019 (Yugipedia). [TEXT] = the printed card text, read out of this engine's own database. [MECH] = a rules consequence derived from card text here, NOT a quote from a player. HONESTY NOTE: the [JK] and [PL] videos only have 2019-era auto-generated captions, which are badly garbled; quotes from them are lightly reconstructed and are marked as paraphrase, never as verbatim. [DF]'s captions are clean and its quotes ARE verbatim.\n\n=== BIG PICTURE \u2014 WHAT THIS DECK IS, AND WHEN ===\nThis is a **June 2019** tournament deck, not a modern Sky Striker. Jesse Kotton \u2014 already a two-time YCS champion \u2014 won the **World Championship Playoff** held on the Friday of the 2019 North America WCQ in Pittsburgh with it, qualifying for the World Championship in Berlin for the third year running [JK video titles + Nerdy Jersey's description: \"Jesse got into the finals of the World Championship playoffs Friday of the NAWCQ which means he is going to the World Championship in Berlin Germany this August\"]. YGOPRODeck bills the list as \"Jesse Kotton (2019 NAWCQ Champion) Deck profile\" [YPD].\n\nIt is a **Mystic Mine stun deck wearing a Sky Striker engine, with a one-card OTK bolted on.** Three axes:\n1) **Lock.** `Mystic Mine` x3, plus nine cards that fetch it (`Terraforming` x2, `Metaverse` x3, `Trap Trick` x3 which fetches Metaverse). You keep ZERO monsters in your MMZ, so the moment the opponent controls even one monster they cannot activate monster effects or declare attacks. [TEXT]\n2) **Grind.** The normal Sky Striker spell engine underneath \u2014 Engage, Widow Anchor, Multirole, the Ace Links \u2014 to bank cards while they are locked.\n3) **Kill.** `Number 39: Utopia Double` + `Double or Nothing!` for exactly 10,000 ATK out of two Level 4 monsters, because a Mine deck that cannot close loses to one top-decked `Twin Twisters`.\n\n[DF], verbatim on why the kill exists at all: *\"in Striker, it's really good because the deck is known for not having enough pressure, right? ... because we're playing so many copies of mine, we want to say, 'Okay, we're not trying to lose the game to twin off top deck. We're trying to end the game.'\"*\n\nKotton's own framing [JK, paraphrase]: he switched off Thunder Dragon because \"people expect me to play Thunder, so why be predictable\"; he expected the playoff field to be Orcust and Sky Striker; and \"the game plan was Double or Nothing and kill them, even in the mirror match \u2014 my game plan was to kill them, explode, not to grind. I can grind, but not as well as other decks.\"\n\n=== HOW THIS DIFFERS FROM THE MODERN / PURE LIST (`cimoooooooo-sky-striker`) ===\nDo NOT pilot this like the modern grind deck. Concretely:\n- **Only 3 monsters in the whole Main Deck**, all `Sky Striker Ace - Raye`. **Zero main-deck hand traps other than `Infinite Impermanence`.** [JK, paraphrase] \"I took the philosophy of most Sky Striker Mine decks, where the hand traps are low value... as a Thunder player I know that against a competent Thunder player a normal hand trap like Ash or Veiler does nothing, and `Called by the Grave` makes them worse. They're obviously bad in the mirror. So: don't play them. Three Raye is all you need.\"\n- **`Infinite Impermanence` x3 is the exception** [JK, paraphrase]: \"the best hand trap, because `Called by the Grave` doesn't stop it, and it has more applications than Veiler.\"\n- **`Cosmic Cyclone` x3 over `Mystical Space Typhoon` / `Twin Twisters`.** Banishing beats destroying in this format, and \u2014 the reason that matters most for YOUR OWN turns \u2014 Cosmic can remove YOUR OWN `Mystic Mine` so you are allowed to attack. See DECISION RULES. [JK] [DF] [PL] all main 3 Cosmic and all give this reason.\n- **`Sky Striker Ace - Kagari` is Limited to 1, `Sky Striker Mecha - Hornet Drones` to 1, `Reinforcement of the Army` to 1, `Upstart Goblin` to 1, `Terraforming` to 2** [BAN]. `Sky Striker Mobilize - Engage!` was still UNLIMITED in this format \u2014 three were legal.\n- **No `Sky Striker Hercules Base`, no `Pot of Desires`.** [DF] verbatim: *\"I didn't play Hercules Base. I don't think that card's necessary.\"* [JK, paraphrase]: Desires \"conflicts with Double or Nothing\" \u2014 banishing 10 can banish your one-of kill pieces.\n- **43 vs 42 \u2014 READ THIS.** Kotton says twice, on camera, that his real list was **43 Main Deck cards**, deliberately, to disguise it as one of his Thunder Dragon combo lists (\"I played 43 at Knoxville that I won with, so I played 43 to make people think I was playing a combo deck\") [JK, paraphrase]; [DF]'s sibling list was also *\"43 cards in the main deck\"* (verbatim). **The YGOPRODeck transcription reproduced here totals 42.** One card is missing from the transcription. The most likely candidate is a third `Sky Striker Mobilize - Engage!` \u2014 Engage was unlimited [BAN] and [DF] says *\"three Engage, three Multirole, three Widow Anchor. Uh, you can't really differ on this\"* \u2014 but that is an INFERENCE, marked **UNSOURCED**. This deck file reproduces the 42 cards that are actually on the source page; if you are comparing against coverage, expect one more Engage.\n\n=== THE MYSTIC MINE LOCK \u2014 HOW IT ACTUALLY WORKS ===\n`Mystic Mine` [TEXT]: \"If your opponent controls MORE monsters than you do, your opponent cannot activate monster effects or declare an attack. If YOU control more monsters than your opponent does, YOU cannot activate monster effects or declare an attack. Once per turn, during the End Phase, if both players control the SAME number of monsters: destroy this card.\"\nThree consequences you must hold in your head every single turn:\n- Sky Striker natively wants an EMPTY MMZ, so you are almost always at zero monsters. Any opponent with a board is therefore fully locked: no monster effects, no attacks. This is why the deck mains three.\n- **It cuts both ways, and it turns off YOUR monster effects too** \u2014 including `Number 39: Utopia`'s attack negation and `Number 39: Utopia Double`'s Quick Effect. If you ever control more monsters than the opponent while your own Mine is up, your kill does not function. [TEXT] [MECH]\n- **Equal counts kill it in the End Phase.** A 0-0 board (common in the mirror) self-destructs the Mine.\nHOW YOU GET IT: `Terraforming` (2) searches it; `Metaverse` (3) is a Normal Trap that takes a Field Spell from Deck and **activates it straight from the Deck**; `Trap Trick` (3) banishes 1 Metaverse from Deck and Sets another Metaverse from Deck, activatable that turn (so Trap Trick is a third-and-fourth Metaverse). [TEXT]\nTHE TRICK THAT MAKES MINE STICK [DF, verbatim]: *\"the main thing you use against it is like Twin Twister and Cosmic Cyclone. They would target us, I would just chain [Metaverse and] set another card. So it was crazy. It would give me advantage over my opponent.\"* Mechanically [MECH]: chain `Metaverse` to their backrow removal and activate a SECOND `Mystic Mine` from the Deck; activating a new Field Spell sends the old one to the GY, so their removal loses its target and you are left with a fresh Mine and a card of profit.\nCAUTION [MECH]: your own `Sky Striker Airspace - Area Zero` and their Field Spell also compete for the one Field Zone. Any Field Spell either player activates replaces yours.\n\n=== THE UTOPIA DOUBLE OTK \u2014 THE WHOLE POINT OF THE DECK ===\nCredit, stated by both pilots: the line was invented by **Ryan Yu**, Kotton's Game Nation teammate and a Dragon Duel World Champion. [JK, paraphrase] \"I can't take credit for this one \u2014 big shout out to Dragon Duel world champion Ryan Yu; he came up with the idea and it got me there.\" [DF, verbatim] *\"I want to give a huge shout outs to my teammates from Game Nation. Uh, Ryan Yu originally came up with the idea, um, and we all played it and play tested it for the event.\"*\n\n**REQUIREMENT: two Level 4 monsters on your field, and the opponent must control at least one ATTACK-position monster.** `Number 39: Utopia Double` grants \"it cannot attack directly\" [TEXT], so you MUST have a monster to swing into.\n\n**THE LINE, step by step** ([DF] verbatim for the sequencing: *\"you go Shark Cannon on level four, normal summon Ray, uh then you make... this card. You make uh you use the effect, detach any material. You summon this and then you add this from deck to hand. It's 5,000. You attack into a monster, you negate it, you activate Double or Nothing. This is 10,000 attack and then it attacks for game. It's a one punch. It's a one card shot.\"*):\n1. **`Sky Striker Mecha - Shark Cannon`**, with 3+ Spells in GY, Special Summons a **Level 4** monster out of the OPPONENT'S GY to your field. It cannot attack \u2014 irrelevant, it is Xyz material. Requires an empty MMZ, so it goes FIRST. [TEXT]\n   **MATCHUP CAVEAT [MECH, confirmed by play-test in this engine]:** Route A needs a Level 4 in THEIR GY. Against a PENDULUM deck their monsters go face-up to the **Extra Deck** instead of the GY when they leave the field, so Shark Cannon often has no legal target at all \u2014 the option simply does not appear. Against Pendulums, plan on Route B from the start.\n2. **Normal Summon `Sky Striker Ace - Raye`** (Level 4, 1500). You now control two Level 4 monsters.\n3. **Xyz Summon `Number 39: Utopia Double`** (Rank 4, ATK 0, 2 materials). PUT IT IN THE EXTRA MONSTER ZONE so your MMZ is empty again and the rest of your Spells stay live. [MECH]\n4. **Utopia Double's Quick Effect: detach 1 material** -> **add `Double or Nothing!` from your DECK to your hand** -> **Special Summon `Number 39: Utopia` from your Extra Deck using Utopia Double itself as material; its ATK becomes DOUBLED (2500 -> 5000)**; materials transfer, so Utopia now holds 2 materials (Utopia Double + the leftover). [TEXT]\n5. **Battle Phase: `Number 39: Utopia` attacks a monster. Negate your OWN attack** with Utopia's own effect (detach 1; \"When a monster declares an attack\" includes its own). Utopia is left with 1 material, so it does not self-destruct. [TEXT]\n6. **`Double or Nothing!`**: \"When a monster's attack is negated: target that monster; it can make another attack during this Battle Phase, and if it does, its ATK is doubled during the Damage Step only.\" -> **attack again at 10,000.** [TEXT]\n\n**DAMAGE MATH \u2014 compute this before you commit.** Battle damage = **10,000 minus the defending monster's ATK**, and only against an ATTACK-position monster (a Defence-position target deals ZERO; there is no piercing) [MECH]. So you need a face-up attack-position monster with **ATK <= 2,000** to kill from 8,000 alone. Fricker's real example [DF, verbatim]: *\"all I had was Ra[ye] in the Shark Cannon, and I Shark Cannon'd back his level four normal summon direct... And I made Utopia double... and I did 8,5[00]\"* \u2014 i.e. 10,000 - 1,500 = 8,500, through a Pendulum Magician board with four negates. If their smallest attack-position body is bigger, top up the difference with a direct attacker (`Sky Striker Ace - Hayate` can attack directly for 1500 [TEXT]) or accept a huge dent and finish next turn.\n**HALF-KILL FALLBACK** [PL, paraphrase]: without `Double or Nothing!` in hand you can still summon Utopia Double into Utopia for a plain **5,000** swing \u2014 \"having done a Double or Nothing you just make this and do 5K\"; [PL] also notes it costs far fewer cards than lining up `Borrelsword Dragon`, \"because that's like 7,500\".\n\n**ROUTE B TO TWO LEVEL 4s \u2014 no Shark Cannon needed.** `Sky Striker Airspace - Area Zero` [TEXT]: \"If this card in the Field Zone is sent to the GY BY A CARD EFFECT: Special Summon 1 'Sky Striker Ace' monster from your Deck\" \u2014 and the only such monster in the Main Deck is Raye. `Sky Striker Mecha Modules - Multirole` sends 1 other card you control to the GY once per turn; point it at your own Area Zero and you get a free Raye from the Deck, plus a Raye Normal Summoned from hand = two Level 4s. [MECH, but this is what Kotton means] [JK, paraphrase]: he runs two Area Zero because \"sometimes you use one for Mine, and afterwards you want to get one for a later turn for the Utopia kill.\"\n**ROUTE C** [MECH, UNSOURCED as a stated line]: `Sky Striker Mecha - Widow Anchor` at 3+ Spells takes control of a face-up Effect Monster until the End Phase; if it is Level 4 it is Xyz material exactly like a Shark Cannon steal.\n**NOT A ROUTE:** the `Sky Striker Ace Token` from `Hornet Drones` is **Level 1** and can never be Rank 4 material. [TEXT]\n\n**PROTECTING THE KILL TURN.** `Multirole`'s send effect also reads \"your opponent cannot activate cards or effects in response to your Spell Card activations for the rest of this turn\" [TEXT]. Fire Multirole FIRST on a kill turn and your Shark Cannon / Cosmic Cyclone / Double or Nothing! cannot be responded to. It does NOT protect the monster effects (Utopia Double's Quick Effect, Utopia's negate) \u2014 those are still `Infinite Impermanence` / `Effect Veiler` bait. [MECH]\n\n**THE THREAT IS WORTH AS MUCH AS THE KILL.** [PL, paraphrase]: \"this being a threat is actually just really good \u2014 if they know you have it, if they see you excavate it, the threat of it modulates how they play, and it makes your backrow better because they have to commit more to the board.\" [DF, verbatim, on the mirror] *\"in the mirror match you don't want to commit your cards to the field, but this forces you to. So either you lose to my Heavy Storm Dusters, my MSTs, and my Cosmic Cyclones, or you just get OTK'd. So either one is like pick your poison.\"*\n\n=== TURN 1 / GOING FIRST (you will often be forced into it) ===\nThis is a going-second deck. [JK, paraphrase] names it as the deck's real flaw: \"the issue I found with Striker being a going-second deck is that you can be forced to go first, and then all those high-impact going-second cards get you blown out. So I wanted to balance that and play cards that are good going first AND second.\"\nGoing first, the job is: **bank Spells in the GY, set the lock, pass with interaction.**\n- Lead with **`Sky Striker Mobilize - Engage!`** (empty MMZ required): search any Sky Striker card; with 3+ Spells already in GY it also draws.\n- **`Foolish Burial Goods` -> `Metalfoes Fusion`** is the fastest way to the 3+ threshold, and Metalfoes Fusion later shuffles itself back from the GY to draw 1. [PL, paraphrase, on why 3 Foolish in his own list] \"the deck has 36 Spell cards and I want my Striker spells to be at max power as soon as possible.\"\n- `Upstart Goblin` and `Reinforcement of the Army` (fetches Raye) are free Spell counts. Note Upstart gives them 1000 LP \u2014 that is 1000 more damage the OTK has to find; do not fire it mindlessly on a turn you might kill.\n- **Set `Trap Trick`.** On their turn (or yours) it fetches `Metaverse`, which activates `Mystic Mine` from the Deck. Remember Trap Trick's clamp: only ONE more Trap that turn, which is exactly the Metaverse it Set. [TEXT]\n- **Set `Infinite Impermanence` in the column of the card you most want dead.** Mirror-match tech [JK, paraphrase]: \"Trap Trick an Impermanence and put it in their Multirole's column \u2014 you negate the monster and you also negate their Multirole.\" [TEXT] confirms: a Set-then-activated Impermanence negates all other Spell/Trap effects in its column for the turn, and columns are shared across the table.\n- End on `Sky Striker Ace - Shizuku` if you made an Ace: her End Phase trigger searches a Sky Striker Spell whose name is not already in your GY. [TEXT]\n- `Sky Striker Ace - Hayate` is NEVER a turn-1 play (no Battle Phase going first, and its mill is a battle trigger). [TEXT]\n\n=== GOING SECOND ===\n1. **Count their monsters first.** If they control 1+ and you control 0, resolving `Mystic Mine` immediately shuts off their whole board \u2014 no monster effects, no attacks. Against a big combo board that is often stronger than trying to remove anything. [TEXT] [PL, paraphrase] \"you just sit there and accumulate resources to make a push for game.\"\n2. **Then decide: lock, or kill.** If they left an attack-position monster with ATK <= 2000, a Level 4 in their GY, and you have Shark Cannon + Raye + a way to be at 3+ Spells, take the kill NOW instead. It ignores negates on the board that do not stop Xyz Summons \u2014 Fricker OTK'd through four negates. [DF]\n3. **`Cosmic Cyclone` is your board-breaker of choice.** [DF, verbatim] *\"when you go second against Orcust, they can just [chain] to protect their counter trap if you MST it and you don't want to be wasting like three cards to kill one that you could just [kill] with a Cosmic Cyclone.\"*\n4. **Sequencing law: every \"control no monsters in your MMZ\" Spell must fire BEFORE any monster lands in your MMZ.** Order is: Engage / Widow Anchor / Afterburners / Jamming Waves / Cosmic Cyclone -> THEN Shark Cannon (which puts a body in your MMZ) -> THEN Normal Summon Raye -> THEN Xyz. [TEXT] [MECH]\n\n=== EXTRA DECK \u2014 ALL 15, WHAT EACH IS FOR ===\nKotton on the shape of it [JK, paraphrase]: \"these take up at least nine spots in the Extra Deck, so I had to cut down. I only played one Kaina and two Hayate \u2014 I didn't need more than two.\"\n- **`Sky Striker Ace - Shizuku` x3** \u2014 Link-1, \"1 non-WATER Sky Striker Ace monster\", arrow top-right. The body you PASS TURN on: opponent's monsters lose 100 ATK/DEF per Spell in your GY, and if she was Special Summoned this turn her End Phase trigger adds a Sky Striker Spell from Deck with a name not already in your GY. Three copies because a Link Monster that leaves the field never returns to the Extra Deck \u2014 the copy count is how many grind turns you buy, not how many you may summon per turn (hard once per turn by name). [TEXT]\n- **`Sky Striker Ace - Hayate` x2** \u2014 Link-1, non-WIND Ace. Can attack DIRECTLY for 1500, and after damage calculation mills a \"Sky Striker\" card from Deck to the GY (fuel for the 3+ threshold and for Kagari to pick up). This is the deck's only recurring clock outside the OTK, and the 1500 that tops up a not-quite-lethal Utopia swing. Kotton kept it at 2 on purpose [JK, paraphrase]: \"I was all-or-nothing most of the time; I didn't need to grind, and after the first few turns it doesn't do much besides attack directly.\"\n- **`Sky Striker Ace - Kagari` x1** \u2014 Link-1, non-FIRE Ace. On Special Summon, add a \"Sky Striker\" Spell back from your GY to hand; gains 100 ATK per Spell in GY. **This is 1 because of the banlist, not by choice** \u2014 Kagari was Limited on the list in force at this event [BAN]. Use it on the Engage/Widow Anchor you most need to re-fire; with only one copy the whole game's recursion runs through it, so do not burn it early on a marginal pickup.\n- **`Sky Striker Ace - Kaina` x1** \u2014 Link-1, non-EARTH Ace. On Special Summon, one opponent monster cannot attack until the end of their turn; also +100 LP per Sky Striker Spell you resolve. The defensive tag-out you take with Raye's Quick Effect on THEIR turn when an attack would otherwise kill you. One copy, by Kotton's own count [JK].\n- **`Number 39: Utopia Double` x1** and **`Number 39: Utopia` x1** \u2014 the kill. See the OTK section. Utopia is ONLY ever summoned via Utopia Double's effect here (it is the doubling clause that makes it 5,000), and Double or Nothing! is searched by Utopia Double, so you never need to draw it. [TEXT]\n- **`Knightmare Phoenix` x1** \u2014 Link-2, \"2 monsters with different names\". Discard 1 -> destroy 1 opponent Spell/Trap (draw 1 if co-linked). Your Extra-Deck answer to a backrow you cannot Cosmic through, and half of the token-cleanup chain below. [TEXT]\n- **`Security Dragon` x1** \u2014 Link-2, \"2 monsters\". While CO-LINKED, once: bounce 1 opponent monster to the hand. Kotton is explicit about why this odd card is here [JK, paraphrase]: the side deck answers `Black Garden`, but after you blow the Field Spell up you are still stuck with the Rose Tokens it gave you \u2014 and tokens in your MMZ switch your entire deck off. \"We had no way to deal with the tokens without it being awkward, so you Link them into this, Phoenix pops the backrow, and Security Dragon bounces something. Otherwise the tokens just sit there doing nothing.\" [PL] independently keeps a slot for exactly this scenario: \"in case someone goes Black Garden and gives you five tokens while they do their combo and then passes turn.\"\n- **`Ningirsu the World Chalice Warrior` x1** \u2014 Link-3, \"2+ Link Monsters\". Once per turn: send 1 card from EACH player's field to the GY \u2014 targetless, destruction-independent removal that goes through most protection. Also the natural dump for two spent Ace Links / tokens. [TEXT] [PL, paraphrase] \"Ningirsu for removing anything that's problematic.\"\n- **`Hiita the Fire Charmer, Ablaze` x1** \u2014 Link-2, \"2 monsters, including a FIRE monster\". Target 1 **FIRE monster in your OPPONENT'S GY** and Special Summon it to a zone this card points to. In this format that means **their `Sky Striker Ace - Kagari`** (FIRE) in the mirror and in Orcust-Striker, or a Salamangreat FIRE Link \u2014 and note their Kagari's own trigger then adds a Sky Striker Spell from **your** GY to **your** hand. [PL, paraphrase] \"Orcust players play Kagari, so I get more Kagari and I can actually grind; Salamangreat Sunlight Wolf, put a monster on top of it to add back my Kagari \u2014 it has an incredible amount of utility.\" The FIRE material it needs is your own Kagari. [TEXT]\n- **`Topologic Bomber Dragon` x1** \u2014 Link-4, \"2+ Effect Monsters\", 3000. While it is on the field, whenever ANOTHER monster is Special Summoned to a zone a Link Monster points to, **destroy every monster in the Main Monster Zones** \u2014 yours are in the EMZ, theirs are not. [TEXT] [PL, paraphrase] \"Bomber is how you lock down the game late \u2014 I love this; Bomber plus Hornet Drones and Shark Cannon is just so hard for the combo decks to play through later in the game.\" Mechanically [MECH]: you hold `Hornet Drones` / `Shark Cannon` as a Quick-Play trigger \u2014 Special Summon a Token or a stolen monster into a linked zone on THEIR turn and wipe every Main Monster Zone on the table.\n- **`Dingirsu, the Orcust of the Evening Star` x1** \u2014 Rank 8, but the clause that matters is \"You can also Xyz Summon this card by using an **'Orcust' Link Monster you control** as material\" [TEXT]. Against Orcust \u2014 one of the two decks Kotton built for \u2014 `Shark Cannon` steals an Orcust Link Monster out of their GY and that stolen body alone makes Dingirsu [MECH]. On summon: send 1 card the opponent controls to the GY; thereafter it eats one destruction per detached material for any card you control. [PL, paraphrase] \"Dingirsu to protect the board.\" Kotton's own comment was only that it is \"just random, good\" [JK, paraphrase] \u2014 treat it as an Orcust-matchup card, not a plan.\n\n=== GRIND & RESOURCE RULES ===\n- **The 3+ Spells threshold governs everything.** Below 3 Spells in GY: Engage does not draw, the Hornet token is 0 ATK, Widow Anchor only negates instead of stealing, Shark Cannon only banishes instead of stealing (so **no OTK**), Afterburners does not also pop backrow. Getting to 3 is a priority on turn 1, and `Foolish Burial Goods` -> `Metalfoes Fusion` is the cheapest way there. [TEXT]\n- **`Multirole` is the mirror's defining card** [PL, paraphrase: \"Multirole is the defining card of the mirror right now; having outs for it is way too important\"]. Its End Phase clause re-Sets Sky Striker Spells from your GY equal to how many you activated that turn while it was face-up \u2014 that is the deck's real card advantage engine. Its first effect doubles as the Area Zero trigger (Route B) and as OTK-turn protection.\n- **Link Monsters never come back.** Every Ace you summon is gone from the Extra Deck for the rest of the game. With 3 Shizuku / 2 Hayate / 1 Kagari / 1 Kaina you have seven Ace summons TOTAL across the whole duel \u2014 spend them deliberately.\n- **Raye's GY effect** revives her when a face-up Ace Link you control is destroyed by battle or removed by an opponent's effect. That is why passing on Shizuku with Raye in the GY is hard to attack profitably. [TEXT]\n- **Do not fire `Upstart Goblin` on a turn you might OTK** \u2014 the 1000 LP you hand them is 1000 more the kill has to cover. [MECH]\n\n=== DECISION RULES \u2014 APPLY THESE FROM THE MENU ===\n1. **Before ANY Sky Striker Spell: is my MMZ empty?** If not, that Spell is illegal this turn. Order all MMZ-conditional Spells before any summon.\n2. **Before declaring an attack, count monsters against `Mystic Mine`.** If YOUR Mine is face-up and you control MORE monsters than the opponent, you cannot attack AND cannot activate monster effects (which kills the Utopia line). Fix it by (a) `Cosmic Cyclone` on your OWN Mine \u2014 pay 1000, banish it [JK, paraphrase: \"Cosmic's one advantage is you pay life and you can destroy your own Field Spell, which came up in my final match; it could have killed them sooner\"], or (b) activating `Area Zero` over it, or (c) `Jamming Waves` / `Afterburners` if it is Set/face-up appropriately.\n3. **Kill check, every turn you have Raye + Shark Cannon (or Route B):** do they control a face-up ATTACK-position monster? Is there a Level 4 in their GY? Do I have 3+ Spells in GY? Is (10,000 - smallest attack-position ATK) + any direct attackers >= their LP? If all yes, take the kill this turn; the deck's whole point is not to give them another draw step.\n4. **If you cannot kill, lock.** Resolve `Mystic Mine` while they have monsters and you have none, then pass with Shizuku and Set interaction.\n5. **Hold `Metaverse` as a counter, not just a searcher.** Chain it to their backrow removal to swap in a fresh Mine and blank their card.\n6. **Set `Infinite Impermanence` in the column of the Spell/Trap you want negated**, not just wherever. The column negate is half the card.\n7. **`Cosmic Cyclone` targeting priority**: a Pendulum Scale or a self-recurring Field/Continuous Spell > a Set card you cannot identify > anything a destruction effect would already handle. Banishing denies GY and Extra-Deck recursion; destruction often does not.\n8. **Never Xyz into the Main Monster Zone if the Extra Monster Zone is free** \u2014 an Extra-Deck monster in your MMZ turns the rest of your deck off for the turn. (This engine runs the newer Master Rule, which allows the MMZ; the 2019 rules did not. See ENGINE CAVEATS.)\n\n=== MATCHUPS ===\n- **ENDYMION / PENDULUM SPELLCASTERS \u2014 THIS IS THE BAD ONE.** [DF, verbatim]: *\"I think if I didn't lose to my worst match up ever, which is Endymion, uh cuz I'm playing Sky Striker, if I didn't lose to that, I think I had the best deck to win the event.\"* Why it is bad, mechanically, against the Endymion list in this repo [MECH, checked against `shadow-spectre-endymion.json` and the printed texts]:\n  * **You feed them.** `Magical Citadel of Endymion`, `Servant of Endymion`, `Mythical Institution` and every Endymion Pendulum bank a Spell Counter *each time a Spell Card is activated* \u2014 by EITHER player. This deck activates 30+ Spells. Every Engage, every Cosmic Cyclone, arms their negates.\n  * **Their boss is untouchable while it holds a counter.** `Endymion, the Mighty Master of Magic`: \"While this card has a Spell Counter, your opponent cannot TARGET it with card effects, also it cannot be destroyed by your opponent's card effects.\" `Widow Anchor`, `Afterburners`, `Infinite Impermanence`, `Shark Cannon` and `Eagle Booster` all target. Hit the pieces, not the boss.\n  * **They can delete your Mine for free.** They main two `Magical Citadel of Endymion`; activating any Field Spell replaces yours. `Metaverse` is your rebuild.\n  * **Citadel dodges destruction but not banishment** \u2014 \"If this card would be destroyed, you can remove 1 Spell Counter instead.\" `Cosmic Cyclone` BANISHES and goes straight through it. This is exactly the reason Fricker mains three [DF, verbatim]: *\"banishes pendulum scales like all the [Endymion] ones that put themselves back. This is really good against that cuz I definitely don't want Servant coming back.\"*\n  * **Shark Cannon is frequently blank here** \u2014 see the MATCHUP CAVEAT in the OTK section. Their Pendulums go to the Extra Deck, not the GY.\n  * **Route B is the kill against them, and it is verified.** A play-test of this exact matchup in this engine: `Multirole` sent `Area Zero` to the GY -> Area Zero Special Summoned `Raye` from the Deck -> Normal Summoned a second `Raye` -> Xyz `Number 39: Utopia Double` into the Extra Monster Zone -> its effect added `Double or Nothing!` and summoned `Number 39: Utopia` at **5,000** -> attacked `Magister of Endymion` (1500 ATK) -> negated its own attack -> `Double or Nothing!` -> attacked again at **10,000** for exactly **8,500 damage**, from 8,000 LP. That is the same number Fricker quotes from the event.\n  * **What does work:** `Mystic Mine`. Endymion floods the board with Pendulum Summons, so they will usually control more monsters than you \u2014 and `Endymion`'s omni-negate is a MONSTER effect, which Mine switches off. Their PENDULUM-ZONE effects are Spell effects and stay live [MECH], so keep Cosmic Cyclone for the scales. And the OTK does not care about negates that only answer activations.\n- **Mirror (Sky Striker).** [JK, paraphrase] the entire side deck is aimed here, \"because my main deck is dedicated to beating combo\". Both players sit at zero monsters, so Mine self-destructs on equal counts; the game is decided by `Multirole` and by whoever resolves the OTK. `Hiita` steals their Kagari. `Trap Trick` -> `Infinite Impermanence` into their Multirole's column blanks it.\n- **Orcust.** The deck Kotton expected in the playoff. They set counter traps, so BANISH rather than destroy [DF]. `Shark Cannon` on a stolen Orcust Link Monster makes `Dingirsu`. Post-side `Mystical Space Typhoon` / `Typhoon` hit their pile of Field and Continuous Spells [JK, paraphrase: \"all the Orcust decks have a lot of Field Spells \u2014 Light Stage, Black Garden, Orcustrated Babel \u2014 plus Continuous Spells, so more backrow removal was really strong going first or second\"]. If they resolve `Black Garden` on you, use the Link package to clear the tokens.\n- **Thunder Dragon.** Kotton's own former deck. Hand traps are near-worthless into it (`Called by the Grave`), which is why there are none; the answer is Mine plus `Infinite Impermanence` [JK, paraphrase] \"you can break the board going second because you hit the [key monster] and then activate Mystic Mine from the Deck\". `Ghost Ogre & Snow Rabbit` comes in from the side.\n- **Any deck that plays no monsters / can go monster-less** blanks Mine and blanks the OTK simultaneously.\n\n=== SIDE DECK \u2014 WHY THESE 15 ===\nKotton's stated design constraint [JK, paraphrase]: \"the side is mostly for the mirror match, because my main deck is dedicated to beating combo\", plus the balancing act of not being blown out when forced to go first.\n- **`Artifact Sanctum` x3 + `Artifact Scythe` x1 + `Artifact Lancea` x1.** Sanctum is a Normal Trap that Special Summons an Artifact from the Deck on the OPPONENT'S turn; Scythe then shuts off their Extra Deck Special Summons for the rest of that turn, Lancea stops all banishing. Three Sanctum is also a legal `Trap Trick` target (Trap Trick needs a second copy in the Deck to Set). [TEXT] [JK, paraphrase] \"when I played Orcust or Salamangreat or Thunder they expect you to go second post-side, so they go first: you search Engage, Sanctum them, they end their turn, then you Engage.\"\n- **`Typhoon` x2 and `Full House` x2 \u2014 deliberately in PAIRS so `Trap Trick` can fetch them** (banish one, Set the other) [TEXT] [JK, paraphrase]: \"you can Trap Trick into your blowout or your single-target removal, whatever the situation is.\" `Full House` is the blowout (destroy 2 face-up + 3 Set Spell/Traps); `Typhoon` is the single-target one that can be activated from the HAND when they have 2+ Spell/Traps and you have none.\n- **`Mystical Space Typhoon` x2** \u2014 more backrow/Field Spell removal for the Orcust-style decks [JK].\n- **`Ghost Ogre & Snow Rabbit` x2** \u2014 the only real hand trap Kotton would side, for Thunder Dragon [JK, paraphrase: \"the two Ogres are just the help against Thunder\"]. [DF] played three and rated it for the rogue matchups (Magician, Draco, Altergeist) and the mirror.\n- **`Dinowrestler Pankratops` x2 \u2014 Kotton says DO NOT USE THESE.** [JK, paraphrase] \"I told [him] not to play these in the mirror match, this card sucks... in the finals I didn't even side it in. It was dead the entire game. It's only average. I don't know if I'd recommend playing it.\" They are in the list, so they are reproduced here; treat them as the weakest two cards in the 60.\n\n=== WEAKNESSES ===\n- **Three Main-Deck monsters.** Lose Raye access and the OTK, the Ace Links and half the Spells go with it. `Reinforcement of the Army` and `Engage` are the redundancy; `Area Zero` is the third.\n- **The kill has hard preconditions**: 3+ Spells in GY, a Level 4 in their GY (or Route B), and an attack-position monster to swing into. A monster-less opponent, or a defence-position wall, turns the OTK off completely.\n- **Mystic Mine is symmetrical and fragile.** It locks YOU whenever you have the bigger board, it self-destructs on equal counts in the End Phase, and any Field Spell either player activates replaces it.\n- **Forced to go first, the going-second cards rot.** Kotton names this as the deck's structural flaw; `Cosmic Cyclone`, `Shark Cannon` and `Double or Nothing!` are all dead into an empty board.\n- **No hand traps at all except `Infinite Impermanence`.** Against a combo deck that resolves its whole line before you untap, your only interaction was the Set Trap Trick.\n- **Very low LP cushion.** Three `Cosmic Cyclone` at 1000 each plus `Upstart Goblin` handing them 1000 means the life totals often favour the opponent.\n\n=== ENGINE CAVEATS (this simulator, not 2019) ===\n- This engine runs the **newer Master Rule**, which lets Fusion/Synchro/Xyz monsters be Special Summoned to the **Main Monster Zone**. The 2019 rules this deck was built under did not \u2014 Extra-Deck monsters had to go to the Extra Monster Zone or a Link-pointed zone. **Always choose the Extra Monster Zone for `Number 39: Utopia Double`**, or you will switch off your own Spells.\n- `Sky Striker Ace - Raye`'s Tribute effect Special Summons an Ace **specifically to the Extra Monster Zone**, so an Xyz sitting in your one usable EMZ blocks the tag-out. Sequence around it.\n- The 2019 Forbidden & Limited List is not enforced by this engine; the copy counts here are the ones that were legal at the event [BAN].",
